==Ancient Greek==

===Alternative forms===
* {{grc-alt|κλέϝος|dial=pho}}

===Etymology===
From {{term|κλέϝος|lang=grc}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|grc}} {{m|ine-pro|*ḱléwos}}. Cognates include Sanskrit {{term|श्रवस्|tr=śrávas|lang=sa|sc=Deva}}, Avestan {{term|𐬵𐬀𐬬𐬀𐬭𐬯|tr=sravah|lang=ae}}, Old Armenian {{term|լու||lang=xcl}}, {{term|լսեմ||lang=xcl}}, Old Church Slavonic {{term|слово|tr=slovo|lang=cu|sc=Cyrs}}, and Old Irish {{term|clú|lang=sga}}. Compare {{term|κλύω||I hear|lang=grc}} and {{term|κλέω|lang=grc}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{grc-IPA|w=κλέος}}

===Noun===
{{grc-noun|κλέους|n|third}}

# [[rumour]], [[report]]
# good report, [[fame]], [[glory]]
# {{context|rare|lang=grc}} bad report, [[disrepute]]

====Inflection====
{{grc-decl-3rd-N-εσ-prx|κλέ|κλέ|κλε|notes2={{w|Homeric Greek|Epic}} plural: {{m|grc|κλέᾰ|tr=-}}, {{m|grc|κλεῖα|tr=-}}}}

